# `Okf.Core.csproj` embeds `skills/*/SKILL.md` into the binary byte for byte, and
# `okf skills install` writes those bytes out again — so an installed skill's digest is
# meant to be the same fact on every machine. A checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` (Git
# for Windows' default) would hand the build CRLF and quietly break that. Pinned to LF
# here rather than trusted to a setting each clone chooses for itself.
skills/*/SKILL.md text eol=lf

# The generated completion scripts are compared byte for byte against these (issue #51);
# a CRLF checkout would fail every golden test for a reason that has nothing to do with okf.
tests/Okf.Cli.Tests/completions/* text eol=lf
